# The build context is sent IN FULL to the daemon before the first Dockerfile
# line runs. (`gcloud builds submit` filters its upload with .gitignore — there
# is no .gcloudignore — and then this file applies again inside Cloud Build.)
# Everything here is bytes nobody needs, and the .env* entries are
# load-bearing for security, not speed.

# Never in an image: secrets. `.env.local` holds the founder's real provider
# keys; an image is pushed to a registry, and a secret in a layer is a secret
# forever, even if a later layer deletes it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Reinstalled cleanly by `npm ci` inside the image. A host node_modules
# (macOS binaries, dev deps) copied in would be both wrong and huge.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# Version control and editor noise.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Not part of the runtime.
test
tests
docs
infra
*.md
*.command
dev.mjs
vercel.json
.vercel
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.test_flow_ref.py
*.py
screenshots
**/screenshots
coverage
*.log
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
